---
title: Southside
servings: 1
tags: [cocktail, gin]
source: Classic cocktail, number 49 on Drinks International's 2026 bestselling classics; method written for this repository
---

In a #cocktail shaker{}(with ice), put @fresh mint{6%leaves}, @gin{2%fl_oz}, @lime juice{0.75%fl_oz} and @simple syrup{0.75%fl_oz}. Shake briskly for ~{10%seconds}, and double strain into a #coupe glass{}(well chilled). Garnish with a @fresh mint{1%leaf}.

> Lemon juice in place of lime is just as common.
